
Project Requirements

Functional Requirements

1. The system shall separate security permissions into domain-specific enums.
2. The system shall create a CourseRight enum for course-related permissions.
3. The system shall create an EventRight enum for event-related permissions.
4. The system shall create a RoomRight enum for room-related permissions.
5. The system shall move existing course permissions from Right.java into CourseRight.
6. The system shall move existing event permissions from Right.java into EventRight.
7. The system shall move existing room permissions from Right.java into RoomRight.
8. The system shall update all references in the codebase to use the new enum names.
9. The system shall preserve the existing behavior of permission checks.
10. The system shall ensure users keep the same access rights after the refactoring.
11. The system shall remove or reduce unrelated permission grouping inside Right.java.
12. The system shall allow future permissions to be added to the correct enum based on subsystem.

Non-Functional Requirements

1. The code shall be easier to read and understand.
2. The code shall be easier to maintain and extend.
3. The refactoring shall not introduce security regressions.
4. The change shall not negatively affect system performance.
5. The code shall follow the existing UniTime coding style.
6. The new enums shall have clear and meaningful names.
7. The implementation shall minimize duplicated code.

Testing Requirements

1. Existing permission tests shall continue to pass.
2. New tests shall verify course permissions using CourseRight.
3. New tests shall verify event permissions using EventRight.
4. New tests shall verify room permissions using RoomRight.
5. Regression tests shall confirm that old permission behavior remains unchanged.
6. Tests shall check that unauthorized users are still denied access.
7. Tests shall check that authorized users still have correct access.

Constraints

1. The change shall be limited to the Security Rights subsystem where possible.
2. Existing user roles and permissions shall not be changed.
3. Database permission values shall remain compatible unless migration is explicitly required.
4. The refactoring shall not break existing APIs or UI behavior.
